WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.155 --> 00:00:02.274
Name the tool you want it to use.

2
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.920
Chatbots now have tools.

3
00:00:06.304 --> 00:00:08.316
But they still work by prediction,

4
00:00:08.366 --> 00:00:11.293
so they only use a tool
when they predict it's needed.

5
00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:14.217
If a topic doesn't look time-sensitive,

6
00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.965
a chatbot may answer from its
training data instead of searching the web

7
00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:19.993
and give you out-of-date information.

8
00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:24.005
And it may convert a file or do maths
with its language model

9
00:00:24.055 --> 00:00:25.418
rather than with code,

10
00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:29.178
and make mistakes or change details
in ways that are hard to notice.

11
00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:34.415
So when you need something recent,
exact or checkable, name the tool:

12
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.689
web search for current information

13
00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:39.614
and code for calculations
or converting files.

14
00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:43.725
Try this. Tell the chatbot
which tools to use. For example:

15
00:00:43.775 --> 00:00:49.104
“Use web search to find the 2026 HEPI
Student Generative AI Survey.

16
00:00:49.154 --> 00:00:53.515
Summarise what it says about how students
use GenAI and link your sources.”

17
00:00:54.037 --> 00:00:57.952
Or: “Use code to merge
these two CSV files together

18
00:00:58.002 --> 00:01:00.051
without changing any of the content.”

19
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:04.968
In the future,
each time you use a chatbot,

20
00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:08.214
consider asking it what tools it used
and how they work.

21
00:01:08.589 --> 00:01:11.144
For example:
“If I ask you to read a website,

22
00:01:11.194 --> 00:01:13.470
what do you actually do?”
